-- title:
--   Deuring: supersingular rational endomorphism ring has ℤ-rank four
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ and algebraic over it (so $k$ is an algebraic closure of the prime field). Let $X$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ that is elliptic, and assume that the group $X(k)$ of points of the associated affine curve has no $p$-torsion: every point $P$ with $p \cdot P = 0$ is $0$. Consider [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k X`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32), the subring of the ring of additive endomorphisms of the point group of the base change of $X$ to $k$ generated by the set of those additive endomorphisms $\alpha$ which are either zero or satisfy the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented k X X` (that is, are represented by rational data over $k$). The assertion is that this subring is, as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, free, finitely generated, and of rank exactly $4$: $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathbb{Z}} = 4$.
--
--   This is Deuring's determination of the endomorphism ring of a supersingular elliptic curve in characteristic $p$: the rank-$4$ case, in which the ring is an order in a quaternion algebra rather than $\mathbb{Z}$ or an imaginary quadratic order. It feeds the identification of this ring with a maximal order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $p$ and $\infty$, and through that the Čerednik–Drinfeld-style counting statements on kernels and relative indices.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_free_and_finrank_rationalEndSubring_eq_four.lean

import Mathlib
